this really depends on the BAM files used. If you didn’t provided the bed file, it should only take more data.
This shouldn’t impact the number of heterozygous positions.
Is the sequencing from a panel of targeted sequencing?

If this is the case you could try to play around with the mufreq model, even if the method is not very well tested and documented.

The error is caused by the lack of BAF position. I have solved the issue in a new version I’m working on, but it’s not ready to be released, and I don’t recommend you to try it out (since many other problems could occur).

Instead you could modify the existing code in sequenza.results and trying to avoid the steps that are causing the problem (it is probably the alternative solution plot…)

Best

Francesco

